Test 6: HSRP Failover (redundancy proof)
Already partially tested during doc 07, but worth re-confirming as part of a full pass:
1. From a Treasurer PC, ping 10.10.30.1 -t (continuous ping, if supported) or repeated single pings
2. On CORE-SW-A: interface vlan 30 → shutdown
3. Watch the ping — should have zero or minimal loss, since CORE-SW-B takes over
4. no shutdown on CORE-SW-A afterward — confirm preempt reclaims Active status via show standby brief

